      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.69,
          "end": 3.33,
          "en": "So how can we tweak this code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.33,
          "end": 5.88,
          "en": "to make sure that we don't run into",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.88,
          "end": 8.883,
          "en": "any optimistic updating problems?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.9,
          "end": 12.96,
          "en": "Well, there of course, again, are different options,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.96,
          "end": 16.32,
          "en": "but one way would be to again use the pipe method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.32,
          "end": 20.16,
          "en": "to add some operators to this observable chain here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.16,
          "end": 24.69,
          "en": "And then we could add the catchError operator here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.69,
          "end": 28.59,
          "en": "to handle potential errors that occur on the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.59,
          "end": 31.17,
          "en": "Here we then get that error object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.17,
          "end": 33.27,
          "en": "that's generated by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.27,
          "end": 35.53,
          "en": "if that request causes an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.57,
          "end": 39.84,
          "en": "and then we can decide how we want to handle it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.84,
          "end": 43.44,
          "en": "Now I will return a new observable generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.44,
          "end": 45.87,
          "en": "with throwError.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.87,
          "end": 48.3,
          "en": "And for that you must make sure that this is imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.3,
          "end": 52.35,
          "en": "because this catchError operator always wants a new",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.35,
          "end": 55.173,
          "en": "observable being returned inside of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.16,
          "end": 58.68,
          "en": "So I'll quickly create a new error here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.68,
          "end": 61.443,
          "en": "to make sure that this is the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.34,
          "end": 64.057,
          "en": "And the error message could be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.057,
          "end": 67.647,
          "en": "\"Failed to store selected place.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.67,
          "end": 72.03,
          "en": "But that's actually not the main thing I want to do in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.03,
          "end": 74.76,
          "en": "Instead, I also want to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.76,
          "end": 79.14,
          "en": "that I roll back my optimistic update here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.14,
          "end": 81.093,
          "en": "if something goes wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.14,
          "end": 84.36,
          "en": "And one way of achieving this would be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.36,
          "end": 86.78999999999999,
          "en": "to go here into catchError",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.78999999999999,
          "end": 90.75,
          "en": "and to update the userPlaces signal here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.75,
          "end": 93.3,
          "en": "To do that, I'll actually change my code up here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.3,
          "end": 95.49000000000001,
          "en": "and I'll get my previous places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.49000000000001,
          "end": 98.55,
          "en": "before we performed the optimistic updating",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.55,
          "end": 100.68299999999999,
          "en": "by simply reading my signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.78999999999999,
          "end": 104.88,
          "en": "As you learned before, this will not set up a subscription,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.88,
          "end": 107.163,
          "en": "it will just read the value once.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.63,
          "end": 111.18,
          "en": "Therefore here we can also simplify this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.18,
          "end": 112.47,
          "en": "and not call update,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.47,
          "end": 116.85300000000001,
          "en": "but just set the observable to this new array like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.84,
          "end": 120.573,
          "en": "That's an alternative to using this update method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.79,
          "end": 125.43,
          "en": "And if we now have an error, we can take advantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.43,
          "end": 127.74,
          "en": "of this previous places constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.74,
          "end": 129.51,
          "en": "which holds the old places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.51,
          "end": 131.013,
          "en": "before we updated them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.85,
          "end": 134.763,
          "en": "to roll back to those previous places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.22,
          "end": 139.62,
          "en": "With that, if you save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 139.62,
          "end": 140.61,
          "en": "here in this app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 140.61,
          "end": 144.21,
          "en": "where we still have this error response on the backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.21,
          "end": 147.99,
          "en": "if I add a place, you see it only appears here briefly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.99,
          "end": 152.52,
          "en": "until that error is caught and then it's rolled back,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.52,
          "end": 155.823,
          "en": "and that's of course better than what we had before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 157.38,
          "end": 159,
          "en": "In addition, I want to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 159,
          "end": 163.86,
          "en": "that we can't add a place we already added before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 163.86,
          "end": 166.35,
          "en": "Therefore, I'll add a check here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 166.35,
          "end": 169.45,
          "en": "and check if in our previous places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 170.46,
          "end": 174.09,
          "en": "we have some place using the built-in some method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 174.09,
          "end": 178.74,
          "en": "which is built into JavaScript and can be called on array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 178.74,
          "end": 180.6,
          "en": "and that then wants a function",
